A cell written in place in two `if`s in a row, in one arm or both, nested, four in a row, then read after them (blind round BM). What the second `if`'s other arm keeps of the first `if`'s value is held on a run through both arms, so it is no holder where the second `if`'s write runs: each write is accepted and runs in place (ownership-v3-kernel.md §6 rule 7, amended 2026-11-22). Its live twin is CellWrittenInTwoIfsLive.
